          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20872 build: Honor o2ib configuration in packaging",
        "message": "LU-20872 build: Honor o2ib configuration in packaging\n\nThe rpm mofed bcond overrode --with-o2ib from configure_args,\nand the deb ext_o2ib/int_o2ib profiles were always enabled\nbecause configure never set @DPKG_EXT_O2IB@/@DPKG_INT_O2IB@.\n\n1) configure: add the default fallback to the OFED search dir,\n   disable external (not in-kernel) o2iblnd on multiple OFED\n   stacks, skip the external checks once it is disabled, and\n   do not force EXTERNAL_KO2IBLND=\"yes\" after detection.\n\n2) rpm/deb: pass --with-o2ib from configure_args/IB_OPTIONS as\n   is, and check after configure that the o2iblnd drivers match\n   the mofed/o2ib bconds or ext_o2ib/noint_o2ib profiles.  The\n   int_o2ib profile becomes noint_o2ib, so in-kernel o2iblnd is\n   expected by default like the rpm o2ib bcond.  If neither\n   o2iblnd is wanted and --with-o2ib is not given, pass\n   --with-o2ib=no.  MOFED rpm build hosts now need --with mofed.\n\nFixes: ec03c9628cae (\"LU-15417 build: find the new path for MOFED 5.5\")\nFixes: 8b1d2a72f10e (\"LU-16967 build: Add in-kernel-ko2iblnd driver\")\nFixes: 95287378fabf (\"LU-16967 build: Separate lnet LND deb packaging\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Xiao Yang <xyang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I5a77db50cf80fac4eb6dda6e73b29fd3e5eda252\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
